  "initial_reflection": {
    "summary": "The run developed a severe HP deficit before the final loss: HP fell from 25 to 1 while repeatedly taking rewards in an HP-loss event, and later combat reduced the recovered HP to single digits. The final Snecko fight also contained a decisive sequencing error, with immediate attacks available but multiple setup and non-damaging actions leaving the enemy alive.",
    "lessons": [
      {
        "category": "EVENT",
        "title": "Exit multi-step HP-loss events early when already wounded",
        "situation": "When an event offers several sequential rewards that each cost HP, especially below roughly one-third health.",
        "lesson": "Take at most the first worthwhile reward, then choose the leave option; do not keep purchasing optional rewards with HP that may be needed for upcoming combats.",
        "evidence_points": [
          "The event began at 25/80 HP, then the selected Riches option reduced HP to 19/80.",
          "The agent continued selecting Success, then A Pick Me Up, and finally left, reducing HP through 13/80, 7/80, and 1/80; the leave option was available at each stage."
        ],
        "reasoning": "The extra rewards did not merely preserve the initial event cost: continuing through the event consumed most of the remaining HP and forced the run to rely on a later shop potion and rest. Leaving after the first reward would have avoided the additional HP losses.",
        "confidence": "high"
      },
      {
        "category": "COMBAT",
        "title": "Prioritize immediate damage over setup at critical HP",
        "situation": "When HP is low, the enemy is already vulnerable, and a damaging card is legally playable with the available energy.",
        "lesson": "Use the available attack before spending actions on setup, card manipulation, or redundant block. In the final fight, Carnage should have been prioritized over Defend, Warcry, Double Tap, and Purity while it was legal at 2 energy.",
        "evidence_points": [
          "On turn 3 against Snecko, with 2 energy and Snecko at 78/114 HP, Carnage was a legal alternative alongside Corruption, Purity, Warcry, and Defend.",
          "After playing Corruption and then Defend, the agent still had 2 energy and Carnage remained legal, but instead played Warcry, selected Carnage, then played Double Tap+ and Purity; Snecko remained alive at 73/114 HP."
        ],
        "reasoning": "At 8/80 HP, prolonging the fight was especially dangerous. The logged state confirms that immediate damage was available, while the chosen sequence spent the turn on effects that did not meaningfully reduce Snecko's HP.",
        "confidence": "high"
      }
    ]
  },
  "review_decision": "HUMAN_TEACHING",
  "human_feedback": "for neows blessing, you should always trade starting relic for boss relic.\r\nduring combat you should factor in enemies' intent as well as vulnerability damage\r\nalso stick to a set plan of deck when picking cards, usually after the first few combats and card rewards you should have a plan already",
